+## Brief items
+
+“Done” below means implemented with focused worker-side tests run; it does not mean a running
+server or live sandbox has been exercised. Complete integration validation remains blocked.
+
+| Item, including owner correction | Status | Evidence / implementation |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 1. Machine -> several nodes -> several agent slots; independent state and compatibility | Done | `crates/aq-node-service/src/layout.rs:124,195,235,241`; `crates/aq-node-service/src/config.rs:21`; `crates/aq-worker/src/bin/aq-worker/service.rs:975`. Two-node/three-agent supervisor and six distinct state/Git/host roots tested. Six native journals preserve node/boot/attempt identity. Native template capacity 1 and larger values both validate; each runner normalizes its journal to one attempt. |
+| 2. One node boot and acknowledged registration per service lifetime, independent of failures | Done | `crates/aq-node-service/src/session.rs:33,107`; `crates/aq-worker/src/bin/aq-worker/service.rs:412`; `crates/aq-worker/src/native/runner.rs:109`. Register-once concurrency/retry tests pass; operation id and boot stay fixed. Legacy v1 compatibility deliberately retains the old per-attempt registration path. |
+| 3. Live per-node count from control; grow/shrink without killing running attempts | Done | `crates/aq-node-service/src/link.rs:180`; `crates/aq-node-service/src/supervisor.rs:329,515,744`. Paused-clock 1->3->1 test passes. V2 fallback caching and missing-count=1 tests pass. No registration on count change. |
+| 4. Independent recovery of several outstanding attempts, held slot only | Partly verified | Held-slot/sibling/node-control test and six-journal old-boot recovery fence test pass. Existing recovery/report/physical-stop code is reused with each node's own credential and slot paths. Actual server terminal replay/host recovery cannot be verified without permitted sockets. |
+| 5. Manual and queued agents share count | Partly verified | `crates/aq-node-service/src/session.rs:120,128`; `crates/aq-worker/src/bin/aq-worker/manual.rs:433,631,684`. Shared local permit, restore and shrink tests pass. Real manual+queued protocol/sandbox exercise is blocked. Server must enforce the same authoritative count. |
+| 6. Preserve multi-node machines; explicit count reduction retires extra nodes as themselves | Done | Node-view layout preserves all old enrollments; `Supervisor::retiring` at `supervisor.rs:323`. Eight-node discovery and six-node recovery-only retirement tests pass. No live machine count was changed. |
+| 7. Packaging, operator docs, final checks and release | Partly verified | Installer/bootstrap use --nodes with --slots compatibility; receiver reads nodes or slots and recognizes nested held state. New manual sections omit max_slots. Packaging: 34 passed, 30 socket-fixture failures, 1 skipped. Clippy, formatting and budget pass. Release built and copied as requested. Full test gates are not green. |
+
+An eight-node machine stays eight nodes after a binary-only update. Each existing
+`slots/K/worker.toml` remains node K's enrollment. Its old state/runtime paths are agent slot 1.
+Additional agent state is `nodes/K/slots/N/current`, with runtime `K-N/{git.sock,host}`. Raising
+agent capacity never enrolls another node. To run only two nodes, explicitly lower `nodes`
+(or the historical `slots` key) to 2 and restart. Nodes 3..8 recover/release using their own
+credentials, admit no new work and do not register a new boot; held recoveries remain held.
+The server/operator separately removes those node records after their attempts are settled.
+Binary-only remote updates preserve the count; an operator can change it locally or run an
+explicit enrollment reconfiguration. No automatic collapse or credential adoption occurs.
+
+Config: new service files serialize `nodes`; old `slots` still means **node count**. Duplicate
+aliases are rejected. `[manual] max_slots` still loads for v1 compatibility, is omitted by new
+writers, and is ignored for slot-aware nodes. Installed native templates remain valid. No
+live configuration or enrollment file was edited.
+
+## Exact verification commands and real results
+
+All cargo tests used the private worktree target, `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8`, `timeout 900` and
+`--test-threads=8`. The hard 900-second rule overrides the brief's conflicting 1700-second
+workspace example. Commands were repeated during implementation; failed intermediate compile
+attempts and corrected assertions are retained in `target/part*.log`. The results below are
+the final relevant runs, not a claim that the full suite passed.
+
+```sh
+CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 timeout 900 cargo test -p aq-node-service --locked -- --test-threads=8
+```
+
+Result: **71 passed, 11 failed, 1 ignored**, exit 101 (`target/node-service-tests.log`). Eight
+fail directly at denied socket creation; two aq-git child fixtures cannot listen; the service
+recovery fixture cannot start its socket-owning attempt. No test was marked ignored to hide
+these restrictions.
+
+```sh
+CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 timeout 900 cargo test -p aq-node-service --locked -- --test-threads=8 --skip git::tests::register_accepts_the_existing_registration_of_this_binding --skip git::tests::register_sends_repo_register_frames --skip git::tests::start_keeps_what_a_live_owner_holds_and_reports_an_early_exit --skip git::tests::start_reclaims_the_socket_and_fence_of_a_killed_aq_git --skip git::tests::stop_and_drop_kill_the_whole_process_group --skip git::tests::the_group_kill_fires_after_the_leader_was_reaped --skip link::tests::edge_refusals_are_not_revocations --skip link::tests::error_carries_status_not_secrets --skip link::tests::sends_bearer_and_access_headers --skip supervisor::tests::a_killed_service_salvages_the_running_attempt_on_restart --skip supervisor::tests::machine_link_posts_each_notice_with_its_slots_credential
+```
+
+Result: **71 passed, 1 ignored, 11 explicitly filtered**, doc tests 0, exit 0
+(`target/node-service-supported-tests.log`). Includes all new per-node supervision, capacity,
+register-once, fallback, local shared-capacity, isolation and retirement tests.
+
+```sh
